    "starterJS": "const textInput = document.getElementById(\"text-input\");\nconst charCount = document.getElementById(\"char-count\");\nconst warningMessage = document.getElementById(\"warning-message\");\n\n// TODO [JavaScript]:\n// 1. Listen for input events on textInput\n// 2. Update charCount.textContent with textInput length\n// 3. Display \"Character limit reached!\" in warningMessage at 100 characters\n// 4. Clear warningMessage when length is below 100\n",
    "solutionHTML": "<div class=\"card\">\n  <h2>Live Character Counter</h2>\n  <textarea id=\"text-input\" placeholder=\"Type your review here (max 100 characters)...\" maxlength=\"100\"></textarea>\n  <p id=\"char-limit-note\">Maximum 100 characters allowed</p>\n  <div class=\"counter-footer\">\n    <span class=\"count-label\"><span id=\"char-count\">0</span> / 100 characters</span>\n    <p id=\"warning-message\" class=\"warning\"></p>\n  </div>\n</div>",
    "solutionCSS": "* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif;\n}\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 24px;\n  background: #f8fafc;\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  align-items: center;\n  min-height: 100vh;\n}\n.card {\n  background: #ffffff;\n  padding: 28px;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);\n  width: 100%;\n  max-width: 420px;\n}\nh2 {\n  margin-top: 0;\n  color: #1e293b;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n}\ntextarea {\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 120px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  resize: vertical;\n  font-size: 14px;\n  outline: none;\n}\n#char-limit-note {\n  font-size: 12px;\n  color: #64748b;\n  margin: 6px 0 0 0;\n}\n.counter-footer {\n  margin-top: 12px;\n}\n.count-label {\n  font-size: 13px;\n  color: #64748b;\n  font-weight: 500;\n}\n/* TODO [CSS]: Style #warning-message with color: #ef4444 and font-weight: 600 */\n#warning-message {\n  margin: 8px 0 0 0;\n  min-height: 20px;\n  font-size: 13px;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  color: #ef4444;\n}",
    "solutionJS": "const textInput = document.getElementById(\"text-input\");\nconst charCount = document.getElementById(\"char-count\");\nconst warningMessage = document.getElementById(\"warning-message\");\n\ntextInput.addEventListener(\"input\", () => {\n  const len = textInput.value.length;\n  charCount.textContent = len;\n  if (len >= 100) {\n    warningMessage.textContent = \"Character limit reached!\";\n  } else {\n    warningMessage.textContent = \"\";\n  }\n});",
    "solutionExplanation": "### Solution Breakdown: Character Counter\n\n1. **HTML Additions**: Fulfills all required element additions matching required IDs.\n2. **CSS Styling**: Implements targeted styling rules, colors, and layout properties.\n3. **JavaScript Logic**: Implements core state management, event listeners, and DOM updates."
